{"page":180,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.20386,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"166 Chapter 3: Derivatives"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09317,"w":0.41967,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 5 Find the derivative of g(t) = tan(5 - sin 2t)."},{"x":0.0585,"y":0.10354,"w":0.1615,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"HISTORICAL BIOGRAPHY"},{"x":0.0585,"y":0.11901,"w":0.10077,"h":0.02365,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Johann Bernoulli (1667–1748)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.12087,"w":0.59302,"h":0.02899,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Solution Notice here that the tangent is a function of 5 - sin 2t, whereas the sine is a function of 2t, which is itself a function of t. Therefore, by the Chain Rule,"},{"x":0.39939,"y":0.15966,"w":0.06387,"h":0.02,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"g′(t) = d"},{"x":0.45283,"y":0.16619,"w":0.12892,"h":0.02076,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dt (tan(5 - sin 2t))"},{"x":0.43575,"y":0.19279,"w":0.14579,"h":0.02238,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= sec2(5 - sin 2t) # d"},{"x":0.74048,"y":0.19328,"w":0.12713,"h":0.01024,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Derivative of tan u with"},{"x":0.5711,"y":0.20111,"w":0.09406,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dt(5 - sin 2t)"},{"x":0.7413,"y":0.20554,"w":0.08112,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"u = 5 - sin 2t"},{"x":0.43576,"y":0.22306,"w":0.23824,"h":0.02702,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= sec2(5 - sin 2t) # a0 - cos 2t # d"},{"x":0.66357,"y":0.22626,"w":0.04727,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dt(2t)b"},{"x":0.74048,"y":0.22843,"w":0.12363,"h":0.02357,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"Derivative of 5 - sin u with u = 2t"},{"x":0.43575,"y":0.25712,"w":0.21503,"h":0.04097,"fs":0.01918,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"= sec2(5 - sin 2t) # (-cos 2t) # 2 = -2(cos 2t)sec2(5 - sin 2t)."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.34121,"w":0.32193,"h":0.01375,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The Chain Rule with Powers of a Function"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.36585,"w":0.58883,"h":0.02815,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"If ƒ is a differentiable function of u and if u is a differentiable function of x, then substitut- ing y = ƒ(u) into the Chain Rule formula"},{"x":0.57597,"y":0.40135,"w":0.05581,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dy dx = dy"},{"x":0.61587,"y":0.40202,"w":0.04374,"h":0.02967,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"du # du"},{"x":0.64369,"y":0.41829,"w":0.01543,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.44171,"w":0.1304,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"leads to the formula"},{"x":0.55477,"y":0.46429,"w":0.12033,"h":0.02727,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"d dxƒ(u) = ƒ′(u)du"},{"x":0.65922,"y":0.47151,"w":0.02167,"h":0.02006,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.50077,"w":0.59306,"h":0.04491,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"If n is any real number and ƒ is a power function, ƒ(u) = un, the Power Rule tells us that ƒ′(u) = nun-1. If u is a differentiable function of x, then we can use the Chain Rule to extend this to the Power Chain Rule:"},{"x":0.49273,"y":0.56405,"w":0.12335,"h":0.02729,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (un) = nun-1du"},{"x":0.60021,"y":0.56694,"w":0.18055,"h":0.02438,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"dx. d du(un) = nun-1"},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.61943,"w":0.59303,"h":0.02984,"fs":0.01407,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 6 The Power Chain Rule simplifies computing the derivative of a power of an expression."},{"x":0.6964,"y":0.65395,"w":0.12545,"h":0.02302,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Power Chain Rule with u = 5x3 - x4, n = 7"},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.65523,"w":0.25324,"h":0.0276,"fs":0.01401,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"(a) d dx (5x3 - x4)7 = 7(5x3 - x4)6 d"},{"x":0.56476,"y":0.65729,"w":0.09062,"h":0.02554,"fs":0.01401,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx (5x3 - x4)"},{"x":0.45801,"y":0.68159,"w":0.20486,"h":0.02238,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= 7(5x3 - x4)6(5 # 3x2 - 4x3)"},{"x":0.45801,"y":0.70461,"w":0.19396,"h":0.01795,"fs":0.01401,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= 7(5x3 - x4)6(15x2 - 4x3)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.73168,"w":0.23031,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":6,"k":0,"t":"(b) d dx a 1 3x - 2b = d dx(3x - 2)-1"},{"x":0.69631,"y":0.76854,"w":0.12545,"h":0.02302,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"Power Chain Rule with u = 3x - 2, n = -1"},{"x":0.4477,"y":0.76982,"w":0.12167,"h":0.02,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= -1(3x - 2)-2 d"},{"x":0.55758,"y":0.77636,"w":0.07837,"h":0.02076,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx (3x - 2)"},{"x":0.4477,"y":0.80112,"w":0.12676,"h":0.01467,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= -1(3x - 2)-2(3)"},{"x":0.4477,"y":0.82176,"w":0.09481,"h":0.02889,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"= - 3 (3x - 2)2"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.86349,"w":0.5414,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"In part (b) we could also find the derivative with the Derivative Quotient Rule."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.88429,"w":0.19012,"h":0.02938,"fs":0.01918,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"(c) d dx (sin5x) = 5sin4x # d"},{"x":0.58322,"y":0.88579,"w":0.21937,"h":0.02357,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Power Chain Rule with u = sin x, n = 5, because sinn x means (sin x)n, n ≠-1."},{"x":0.50165,"y":0.89327,"w":0.04796,"h":0.02008,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dxsin x"},{"x":0.42949,"y":0.92001,"w":0.09441,"h":0.01421,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= 5sin4xcosx"}]}